FLEX public headers (compile-time only; FLEX implementation is not vendored)
  URL: https://github.com/FLEXTool/FLEX
  Commit: ac50a6d36b738a15a6d3b6b51683d8a152319f59
  Version: 4.7.0
  Vendored: Classes/Headers/*.h

Local build adaptations:
  - Echo and Reflex Swift sources are compiled into the same libreflex Swift module,
    so Reflex's redundant `import Echo` lines are removed.
  - FLEX 4.7 compatibility shims dynamically probe newer FLEX mirror selectors
    and fall back to the selectors available in the pinned 4.7 public headers.
  - Echo's four swift-atomics accesses in ClassDescriptor.swift are replaced by
    CEcho C11 atomic helpers with the same seq_cst, release, and relaxed orderings.
    Int.AtomicRepresentation is layout-compatible with its integer storage; the
    adapted stored field uses Int at the same pointer-sized layout.
  - CEcho's module map exposes only declaration-safe headers; ImageInspection.h
    is excluded because it contains function definitions that break object emission.
  - Pointer-authentication helper declarations used by Swift are visible to the
    Clang importer on both build slices, while arm64e-only definitions stay guarded.
  - SignedPointer.swift uses one generic signing accessor and applies arm64e
    stripping for ProtocolDescriptor, ValueWitnessTable, and TypeContextDescriptor.
  - CEcho and FLEX module maps are supplied locally for Theos Swift compilation.
